	"Consumers": [],
	"Description": "Every Okta kit detection: one alert with 49 producers (scheduled searches), one per detection, all with the same 16 fields (_alert_title, _alert_priority, _alert_name, _alert_risk, _vendor, _product, _category, _subcategory, user, src_ip, target, eventType, _mitre_tactic, _mitre_technique, context, published).\n\nGroups (label on each scheduled search; _category in the event): authentication-sessions (24), admin-configuration-changes (13), account-mfa-changes (5), threats-platform (5), modification-feed (1: a high-volume, risk-scored audit stream of configuration and account changes) and kit-health (1: Target Key Order Changed, Critical, _category Kit Health).\n\nNo consumers are attached. Next step after install: add a consumer flow (email, Slack, Teams, webhook, Jira, ...); filter on Contents._alert_priority, _category or _alert_name in the flow if different detections go to different places. Alert events are also written to the shared _alerts tag (Contents._vendor is Okta), so you can search them without a consumer. Disable a producer to turn off one detection. Each producer run raises at most 3 alert events. The search behind each alert event is kept for 7 days.",
	"Disabled": false,
